@startuml MARS_OPS_State_Machine_Diagram
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam stateFontStyle bold
skinparam shadowing false

title MARS-OPS Mission Lifecycle - State Machine Diagram

[*] --> Created : new Mission(duration)\n[status = null, elapsed = 0]

state "Created (Unsubmitted)" as Created {
    Created : status = null
    Created : elapsed = 0
    Created : failureReason = ""
}

state submissionCheck <<choice>>

Created --> submissionCheck : colony.submitMission(mission)

submissionCheck --> ASSIGNED : [activeMission == null &&\n envAllowed &&\n mission.validateRequirements() &&\n agentManager.canProvide(mission) &&\n facilityManager.canProvide(mission)]\n/ agentManager.provide(mission);\n  mission.assignAgents(agents);\n  facilityManager.provide(mission);\n  colony.activeMission = mission

submissionCheck --> FAILED : [rejection condition met]\n/ rejectMission(mission, reason);\n  pastMissions.add(mission)

note on link
  **Submission Rejection Causes (Never Becomes Active):**
  1. Another mission is already active (activeMission != null)
  2. Dust storm blocks surface ExplorationMission
  3. Comm disruption blocks communication-dependent Mission
  4. Invalid mission parameters (!mission.validateRequirements())
  5. Suitable/available agents lacking or insufficient battery/high fatigue (!agentManager.canProvide)
  6. Insufficient colony-wide operational resources/equipment (!facilityManager.canProvide)
  *(All-or-nothing: no resources consumed, no agents locked)*
end note

state ASSIGNED {
    ASSIGNED : status = MissionStatus.ASSIGNED
    ASSIGNED : elapsed = 0
    ASSIGNED : activeMission = this
    ASSIGNED : assignedAgents marked unavailable & relocated
    ASSIGNED : required resources & equipment deducted
}

state IN_PROGRESS {
    IN_PROGRESS : status = MissionStatus.IN_PROGRESS
    IN_PROGRESS : 0 < elapsed < duration
    IN_PROGRESS : do / agents update fatigue / battery per timeUnit
}

ASSIGNED --> IN_PROGRESS : colony.advanceTime(timeUnit)\n[envAllowed]\n/ mission.tick(timeUnit)\n  (status = IN_PROGRESS; elapsed += timeUnit)

ASSIGNED --> FAILED : colony.advanceTime(timeUnit) [envHazard]\nOR mission.fail(reason)\n/ fail(reason); pastMissions.add(this);\n  agentManager.release(this); activeMission = null

IN_PROGRESS --> IN_PROGRESS : colony.advanceTime(timeUnit)\n[envAllowed && elapsed + timeUnit < duration]\n/ mission.tick(timeUnit) (elapsed += timeUnit)

IN_PROGRESS --> COMPLETED : [elapsed >= duration]\n/ elapsed = duration; mission.complete();\n  pastMissions.add(this);\n  agentManager.release(this);\n  activeMission = null

IN_PROGRESS --> FAILED : colony.advanceTime(timeUnit) [envHazard]\nOR mission.fail(reason)\n/ fail(reason); pastMissions.add(this);\n  agentManager.release(this); activeMission = null

note right of IN_PROGRESS
  **Runtime Failure Causes:**
  - Dust storm hits active ExplorationMission
  - Comm disruption hits comm-dependent Mission
  - Equipment failure / Rover breakdown / Battery depletion
end note

state COMPLETED {
    COMPLETED : status = MissionStatus.COMPLETED
    COMPLETED : elapsed == duration
    COMPLETED : entry / restore repaired target (if RepairMission)
    COMPLETED : entry / rescue stranded agent (if RescueMission)
    COMPLETED : entry / assigned agents released & returned to originLocation
}

state FAILED {
    FAILED : status = MissionStatus.FAILED
    FAILED : failureReason != ""
    FAILED : entry / record failureReason in pastMissions
    FAILED : entry / release assigned agents (if any)
}

note bottom of FAILED
  **Terminal State:**
  Failed missions cannot be retried (tick() is ignored).
  A new Mission instance must be created for another attempt.
end note

COMPLETED --> [*]
FAILED --> [*]

@enduml
